# Deployment topology — WHERE this repository gets deployed.
#
# Copy to `deploy.env` (gitignored) on any machine that deploys, and to
# $APP_DIR/deploy.env on the server itself. Nothing here is secret: the domain
# and the host address are published by DNS anyway. It is kept out of git so the
# repository states how to deploy without stating where — the same tree can be
# pointed at a staging box by changing this file alone.
#
# Application/runtime configuration is a separate concern and lives in `.env`
# (see .env.example): database credentials, ADMIN_TOKEN, IP_HASH_SALT.

# ─── Used by scripts/deploy.sh, on a developer machine ──────────────────────
# Required. No default on purpose: a wrong guess would deploy somewhere real.
DEPLOY_HOST=
DEPLOY_USER=root
BRANCH=main

# ─── Used by scripts/server-deploy.sh, on the server ────────────────────────
# The domain the site is served on. Required.
SITE_DOMAIN=
# Space separated, optional. Each one 301-redirects to SITE_DOMAIN, preserving
# the path. Leave empty to generate no redirect vhost at all.
REDIRECT_DOMAINS=
# acme.sh installs certificates into $CERT_DIR/<domain>/{fullchain,privkey}.pem
CERT_DIR=/root/cert
# The path nginx proxies to the loopback VLESS+XHTTP inbound (Xray). Required,
# no default: a guessable value defeats the point of it being secret. Leading
# slash, no trailing slash — e.g. /a73fa993963558096f061a22, generated with
# `openssl rand -hex 12`. Keep it in sync with the Xray inbound's
# streamSettings.xhttpSettings.path (which needs the trailing slash added back).
XHTTP_PATH=
# Polled after `docker compose up` to decide whether the deploy succeeded.
HEALTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/
HEALTH_RETRIES=30
